context_portal/

# Fixed, crash-released offload-metrics OS-lock identity. Same reasoning as
# the bridge and registry locks above: the file survives process exit by
# design, only the ownership is transient.
memory/offload_metrics.local.jsonl.lock

# Machine-bound project registry row for the local checkout. docs/DESKTOP.md
# calls this runtime state seeded below the external profile root, and it
# carries an absolute repo_root -- the exact class of hardcoded machine path
# 5375f0c3 removed. The four tracked sibling rows point at C:\Users\nukei and
# are stale history, not a precedent to follow.
projects/daedalus.json

# Fleet analysis scratch. The .md dossiers under runs/analysis/ are the
# deliverable; the .py files beside them are one-off probes and mutation
# harnesses. Two got committed with G1-SEC-01 as exploit evidence and the
# Effect Registry scanner correctly refused them: a script with a main()
# that spawns subprocesses IS an unregistered effectful entrypoint, and
# runs/ is scanned by design. The durable record of that exploit is the
# payload and canary result quoted in the packet's commit message.
runs/analysis/**/*.py
runs/analysis/**/tmp/
runs/analysis/**/_scratch/
runs/analysis/**/*.txt
memory/events.local.jsonl.lock
